  "details": "I know there is AFK avatar, but i think we need another solution if we don't want change much or have for very short toilet or controller or headset problem. Or when VR system went out of control, or you are out the tracking area.\n\nWhy should we switch to AFK avatar for that?\n\nOpen menu and click here to enable \"offline pose\". This pose mode will make sure your avatar will go in normal standing position with arms down and facing forward. You can still move around but the pose stay fixed. If you're sitting on the chair there, it will stay in default sitting pose. It's almost like you're just disabled the VR system.\nThe off line pose can also activated with keyboard key, if your controller is out of the control / broken / battery dead... It's sort of emergency pose. (A dead controller cannot use menu - so select the AFK avatar is not possible!)\n\nThat will avoid flipping over or make it embarrasing pose when you take off your headset for short time or controller is broken.",
